WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:10.880
The history of gaming extends 5,000 
years into the past to ancient Egypt.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:15.250
Ancient games foretold the 
futures of men and kings.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.950
They were magic ceremonies that 
determined a person's fate.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.930
These ceremonies were known 
as the "Shadow Games."

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.630
In the present, a young boy 
solves the Millennium Puzzle.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.960
He becomes the heir to the Shadow Games.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.050
This boy possesses two hearts - 
one of light and one of darkness.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.960
He is known as "Yu-Gi-Oh."

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.310
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:57.220
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:03.970
Game cartridges are stacked 
in the corner of the room

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:10.670
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.770
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:19.140
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:26.070
You don't change your 
facial expression at all

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:32.320
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:39.590
These feelings don't reach 
you, don't reach you

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:46.330
What is truly precious?

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:55.540
The Fearsome Blue-Eyes White Dragon

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:02.480
It's your turn, Jonouchi.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:07.030
What are you doing, Jonouchi?

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:10.570
You don't know about Duel Monsters?

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:11.700
What's that?

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.340
You're so annoying!  Be quiet and watch!

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:20.100
It's a game where you strategically assemble 
your monster and spell cards to battle.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.330
I made my choice.  I'll battle with this!

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.640
Cards have attack and defense points.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.150
You win if you eliminate 
your opponent's life points.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.140
Yugi, it's your turn.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:33.110
Right.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.580
It's my turn.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:36.800
I'll attack with this.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.950
How can you casually play 
such a powerful card?

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.540
I lost in an instant!

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.220
You're too weak, Jonouchi.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:48.020
It's not that I'm a strong player.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:53.150
My grandpa owns a game shop and is really 
into card games, so I can get powerful cards.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.070
We're going to your place after school.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:01.330
Sure.  I'll bet my grandpa will 
show you his super rare card.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.640
Super rare card?

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.550
Can he possibly be talking about...

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.410
Grandpa, I'm home!

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.780
You're all together today.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.420
Can you show them your incredible card?

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.030
Do you mean that special card?

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:22.110
Please!

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:23.520
Please!

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:27.760
I guess I have no choice.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:31.500
You should feel special because 
this is my prized possession.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.630
Here it is.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:36.860
This is Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.410
It's a super ultra rare card.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.250
Awesome!

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.330
This thing?  Really?

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:49.180
Only four copies exist in 
the world.  It's priceless.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.350
Gramps, I'm gonna buy some cards.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:52.770
I won't sell this!

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.220
I can't afford that.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:59.110
I want packs that contain powerful cards.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:02.800
Welcome.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.630
You're...

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.240
Kaiba!

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:13.440
What is Kaiba Corporation's heir doing here?

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:16.750
I heard Yugi's grandfather is a card fanatic.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:20.120
Kaiba, you also play Duel Monsters?

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.550
Perfect!  You can play with us.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.470
Cut it out.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:26.920
You don't have the right to play against me.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.090
What?

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:33.280
I have the skills to win the Duel 
Monsters national championship.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:37.060
You and I are on totally different levels.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.870
How dare you!  You can't talk to me that way!

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:42.430
Calm down, Jonouchi.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:43.510
But...

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.040
He's super annoying.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.780
Does this store have any worthwhile cards?

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.190
What?

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:56.080
What is Blue-Eyes White Dragon 
doing in a place like this?

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:00.110
I can't believe I found it!

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:02.380
Time's up.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:04.530
This isn't for sale.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:16.870
I'll trade all these cards for 
your Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.730
Wow!

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:22.410
No.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.420
If you won't trade, then name your price!

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:30.650
I'll pay whatever you want!

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:39.150
Kaiba, the reason why I won't give you 
this card isn't because it's powerful.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:44.250
A very dear friend gave me this card.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:48.110
This card is as valuable as our friendship.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:52.070
No matter how much you offer, 
I'll never part with this card.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:53.930
What?

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:57.850
You would feel the same 
even if it was a weak card.

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:02.680
Exactly.  Your heart lives 
inside your precious cards.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:07.580
I'm leaving.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:14.440
Cards have heart?  That's ridiculous.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.100
Cards are power!

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.100
I'll do whatever it takes to get that card.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:25.100
Master Kaiba, we have acquired 
the remaining three cards.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.690
So that old man has the final card.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:28.750
Yes.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.620
Welcome-

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:44.090
Master Kaiba challenges you 
to a duel, Sugoroku Muto.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:47.100
What if I decline?

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.360
We will force you to accept.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:54.120
That boy doesn't understand.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.630
I must teach him about 
the heart of the cards.

00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:57.850
C'mon, Anzu!

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.510
Whatever!

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:03.010
Gramps, I'm back to buy more cards.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.140
Gramps?

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:07.010
Grandpa, I'm home.

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:08.230
Is he out?

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:10.750
He forgot to lock the front door.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.540
Hello?

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:17.210
Yugi?

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:18.770
Kaiba?

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.440
I have your grandfather.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:25.200
Come to my building to pick him up.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:28.000
What do you mean, Kaiba?

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:41.920
Grandpa!

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:44.360
Grandpa, pull yourself together!

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:48.220
Yugi, I'm sorry.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:53.000
I wanted to teach him about 
the heart of the cards, but...

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.240
Grandpa!

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:57.310
You're late.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.560
What did you do to him?

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:05.310
We had a duel and wagered 
our most valuable cards.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:10.950
I guess the virtual simulator that 
I invented was too much for him.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:14.550
You must have cheated!

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:18.190
Never.  This card proves that I won.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.560
Grandpa's most cherished card!

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:29.650
Since a deck can only have three copies per 
card, the fourth could be used against me.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:30.800
The fourth?

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:34.130
My Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.310
Grandpa!  Hang in there!

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:39.310
How horrible!

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:41.810
Yugi, take this.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:43.880
Grandpa.

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:48.100
I dueled him using this deck.

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:50.840
I lost, but my spirit is in these cards.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:54.280
You have what it takes to beat him.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:57.830
Teach him the true heart of the cards.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:01.040
But I can't leave you like this, Grandpa.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:02.170
Interesting.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:07.120
If you want to avenge your grandfather, 
I'll accept your challenge.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:10.160
Yugi, battle him!

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:14.440
Leave Gramps to us.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:18.790
Teach him what real dueling is all about!

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.420
Fight him, Yugi!

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:21.640
You guys...

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:27.790
I used to get into fights all the time, but 
you changed me.  So you can change him!

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:33.800
Okay, Grandpa.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.930
I'm counting on you, Yugi.

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:38.040
Everyone, put your hands out.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:41.430
This is the symbol of our friendship.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:43.600
What's this?

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:50.180
The ink will easily wash off, but this 
ring will always remain in our hearts.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:59.840
Jonouchi, Honda and I will stay with Grandpa.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:01.660
You go support Yugi.

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.330
Okay.  Take care of him, Anzu.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:07.160
We'll play using my special rules.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:08.810
We start with 2000 life points.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:12.300
If your life points drop to 0, you lose.

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:20.470
Virtual system on!

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.160
What?

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:52.260
Kaiba, I believe in my grandfather's 
deck and will defeat you.

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.300
The duel begins!

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:10.690
I go first.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:13.460
Hitotsu-Me Giant in attack position.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:22.800
The monster has become real!

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:26.710
This is my virtual simulation system.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:30.680
This is what my grandfather lost against.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:33.680
I'll take it on.  It's my turn.

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:35.870
Winged Dragon, Guardian of the Fortress #1!

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:38.050
In attack position!

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:43.370
What?

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.620
Wow!  What is this?

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:48.760
Fireball Attack!

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:55.940
Big brother!

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:00.540
All right!  Well done!

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:04.280
It wouldn't be fun without a handicap.

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:06.280
I'll attack with this card!

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:13.390
Saggi the Dark Clown?   It can't 
win with those attack points.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:19.630
Winged Dragon has 1400 attack points while 
my monster has 600, so my monster can't win.

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:22.900
But I'll also play this card!

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:24.350
That's a spell card.

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:27.570
Exactly.  Negative Energy Generator!

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:30.940
It triples a Dark Attribute 
monster's attack points.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.990
Saggi the Dark Clown attacks.

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:39.060
Dark Light!

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:46.690
That's the destructive 
power of my combo attack!

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:50.540
Kaiba understands every aspect of this game.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:57.090
But my grandfather is a game master who 
poured his heart into making this deck.

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:59.630
It must contain a secret strategy.

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:05.380
I can't beat Saggi the 
Dark Clown with this card.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:09.440
I'll have to play a different monster 
in defense position and try to survive.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:14.810
Dark Light!

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:20.420
What are you doing?

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:32.940
The dying old man left you that deck.

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:37.170
I can hear his dying breath 
coming from those cards.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:41.380
My grandfather entrusted me with these 
cards because he believes in me.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:45.550
I can hear the heartbeat 
of his passionate spirit.

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:49.910
Kaiba, do you believe in your cards?

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:53.820
I believe in these cards.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:02.430
I drew Gaia the Fierce Knight.

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:04.440
It has 2300 attack points.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:05.670
Attack Saggi the Dark Clown!

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:06.680
What?

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:11.670
Spiral Shaver!

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:14.880
It's destroyed!

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:19.720
You did it, Yugi!

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.180
The battle isn't over yet.

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:25.200
The ending is already decided.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:30.300
Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:34.960
No way!

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:38.030
I thought he tore up Gramps's card.

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:41.310
Blue-Eyes White Dragon attacks!

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:44.320
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.490
Gaia the Fierce Knight is destroyed.

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:01.440
I'll do whatever it takes to get what I want.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:05.520
I have two more Blue-Eyes in my deck.

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:07.260
There's no way you can win.

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:13.700
Are you planning to play defense 
until you run out of cards?

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:17.810
I drew my second Blue-Eyes.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:23.250
Just admit defeat, Yugi!

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.700
Yugi...

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:34.680
I won't give up, Grandpa.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:38.990
The spell card Swords of Revealing Light.

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:43.490
It stops all monsters on your field 
from attacking for three turns.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.880
That is pointless.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.910
Even with a three-turn delay, 
you still can't do anything.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:54.090
Kaiba is right.

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:56.980
I don't see the point of these three cards.

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:59.740
How can I fight with these?

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.420
This isn't like you, Yugi.

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:12.490
Everything has meaning, just like the 
Millennium Puzzle you worked hard to assemble.

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:14.500
The Millennium Puzzle?

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:19.190
Just like you put those pieces 
together, do the same with the cards.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:20.720
Grandpa!

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:23.630
Like pieces of a puzzle.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:26.680
Exodia?

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:30.340
Does this deck contain Exodia?

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:35.170
In Duel Monsters, there is one 
invincible monster that can only be

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:38.840
summoned by gathering five specific cards.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:43.520
But to this day, no one has 
managed to gather the five cards.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:48.030
It's your turn!  Hurry up and draw your card!

00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:49.540
I draw!

00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:54.050
I've gathered four cards.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:56.850
No matter what you draw, 
it won't change anything.

00:16:57.130 --> 00:17:02.180
It's my turn.  My new monster will 
attack your defending monster.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:05.780
Judge Man!  2200 attack points!

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:13.260
Dark Magician.

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:18.890
Blue-Eyes will just destroy it if I place it in 
defense position, so I'll have it attack Judge Man.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.590
Black Magic!

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:27.260
Judge Man is destroyed.

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:33.510
That small amount of damage 
doesn't hurt me at all.

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:36.520
Your seal will disappear in one turn.

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:41.520
I drew my third Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:47.520
Attack Dark Magician!

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:57.670
Yugi, draw your final card.

00:17:57.670 --> 00:18:02.420
All three Blue-Eyes will 
attack you next turn.

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:05.670
No matter what you draw, it's all over!

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:07.330
Yugi!

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:12.450
These cards are essential in 
forming Exodia the Forbidden One.

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:18.450
But the odds of drawing the final card 
on the last turn is extremely low.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:26.220
The cards are moving away.

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:30.970
No, it's me.  I'm scared to draw a card.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.160
This ink drawing...

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.930
This is the symbol of our friendship.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.180
Yugi, you're not alone.

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.710
This ring unites us together.

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:48.680
Thank you.  I'm no longer afraid.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:52.820
You've accepted your fate and 
reached out towards despair.

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:56.360
You're wrong.  I now have hope.

00:18:56.890 --> 00:18:58.790
The card I drew was...

00:18:59.590 --> 00:19:01.930
Exodia the Forbidden One.

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:03.930
What?

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:06.940
I've gathered all five cards.

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:21.180
Impossible!  Exodia?

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:23.170
You performed a miracle?

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:26.810
The fires of rage!  Exodo Flame!

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:40.670
He did it!  Yugi won!

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:43.910
What?  My brother lost?

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:48.780
No matter how strong your cards, they're 
meaningless if they have no heart.

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:52.510
Miracles happen when your 
heart and cards become one.

00:19:52.510 --> 00:19:56.390
Impossible.  How could I lose?

00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:59.720
Kaiba, I will destroy the evil in your heart.

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:01.970
Mind Crush!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:08.990
The evil in your heart has been destroyed.

00:20:12.130 --> 00:20:13.790
You've regained consciousness.

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:15.480
Yugi...

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:23.080
Master Pegasus, Seto Kaiba of Kaiba 
Corporation has been defeated in a duel.

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:36.760
Jonouchi has started playing 
Duel Monsters seriously?

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:39.830
Can he keep up with Yugi's 
grandfather's training?

00:20:40.140 --> 00:20:44.170
That's when Yugi receives a videotape.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.470
I think that's Pegasus Crawford.

00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:50.800
You're going to duel against the videotape?

00:20:50.800 --> 00:20:53.050
What?  A Shadow Game?

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:57.120
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Illusionist Faceless Mage's Trap

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:59.430
Duel, standby!

00:21:00.930 --> 00:21:09.330
The flask glistens

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:17.180
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:26.160
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:33.930
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:35.630 --> 00:21:39.760
Shower of happiness

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:43.880
I will shower you with it

00:21:44.200 --> 00:21:52.150
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:56.390
Shower of happiness

00:21:56.650 --> 00:22:00.510
You are not alone

00:22:00.890 --> 00:22:07.230
You're protected by a 
giant ring of friendship
